---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const description =
	'About Stephen McCruden: field engineering, Kubernetes, infrastructure automation, observability, and reliable systems.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description} />
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main>
			<header class="introduction">
				<p class="eyebrow">About me</p>

				<h1>I’m Stephen McCruden.</h1>

				<p class="lede">
					I’m a field engineer focused on reliable infrastructure, automation,
					and the operational work required to keep important systems running.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section aria-labelledby="professional-work">
				<h2 id="professional-work">Professional work</h2>

				<p>
					I support mission-critical public-safety communications infrastructure.
					My work includes system upgrades, lab validation, troubleshooting,
					documentation, and coordinating technical work across teams and customer
					environments.
				</p>

				<p>
					Working on systems where reliability matters has shaped how I approach
					engineering: understand the dependencies, document the procedure, validate
					the result, and prepare for what happens when something fails.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="homelab">
				<h2 id="homelab">The homelab</h2>

				<p>
					My primary engineering project is a three-node Kubernetes platform running
					on Proxmox. It is designed as a reproducible environment for learning and
					practicing infrastructure engineering—not simply as a collection of
					self-hosted applications.
				</p>

				<ul>
					<li>Terraform provisions the virtual infrastructure.</li>
					<li>Ansible configures and hardens the operating systems.</li>
					<li>Flux manages Kubernetes resources through GitOps.</li>
					<li>Cilium provides cluster networking and policy enforcement.</li>
					<li>Prometheus and Grafana provide metrics and visibility.</li>
					<li>Rebuilds and failure tests validate the platform’s design.</li>
				</ul>

				<p>
					The entire cluster has been destroyed and rebuilt without undocumented
					manual intervention. The next stages include persistent storage,
					centralized logging, disaster-recovery testing, and additional stateless
					applications.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="approach">
				<h2 id="approach">How I approach engineering</h2>

				<div class="principles">
					<article>
						<h3>Reproducibility</h3>
						<p>
							If a system cannot be reconstructed predictably, its recovery
							process is incomplete.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3>Observability</h3>
						<p>
							A healthy-looking system is not enough. Its behavior and failure
							signals need to be visible.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3>Documentation</h3>
						<p>
							Architecture decisions, procedures, incidents, and lessons should
							outlive the person who discovered them.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3>Failure testing</h3>
						<p>
							Backups, automation, and high availability only become trustworthy
							after they have been tested.
						</p>
					</article>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="direction">
				<h2 id="direction">Where I’m headed</h2>

				<p>
					I’m building toward site reliability, platform, and infrastructure
					engineering roles. This site is where I document that work openly:
					the architecture, implementation, failures, recoveries, and decisions
					behind the finished systems.
				</p>

				<div class="actions">
					<a class="button primary" href="/blog">Read the blog</a>

					<a
						class="button secondary"
						href="https://github.com/Stephen-McCruden"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noreferrer"
					>
						View my GitHub
						<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.introduction {
		padding: 2rem 0 4rem;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--accent-dark);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.introduction h1 {
		font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.lede {
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-size: 1.15rem;
	}

	main > section {
		padding: 3rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}

	main > section h2 {
		font-size: 2rem;
	}

	.principles {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.principles article {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 8px;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65);
	}

	.principles h3 {
		font-size: 1.35rem;
	}

	.principles p {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.button {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
		border: 2px solid var(--accent);
		border-radius: 6px;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.primary {
		background: var(--accent);
		color: white;
	}

	.primary:hover {
		background: var(--accent-dark);
		color: white;
	}

	.secondary {
		background: white;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.introduction {
			padding-top: 1rem;
		}

		.principles {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
